    <statement><p>Find all critical points of the function <m>f(x)=x^2-{7}x+{2}</m></p>
<p><m>x=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3.5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 




Let <m>f(x)=x^2-{7}x+{2}</m>. Then <m>f'(x)=2x - {7}</m>. 


Since <m>f(x)</m> is differentiable everywhere, the critical points are the solutions of <m>f'(x)=0</m>.  Then  <m>2x - {7}=0</m>, 


implies <m>2x={7}</m>  or  <m>x=\frac{7}{2}</m>, 


and <m>x=3.5</m> is the lone critical point of <m>f</m>.



</solution>
